<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trans-mūto</span></b> , āre,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to change</i>, <i>shift</i>, <i>transmute</i> (<b>poet.</b>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commuto, verto, converto): transmutans dextera
					laevis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 488</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(fortuna) transmutat incertos honores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 29, 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To transfer</i>, <i>remove</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aegros ad alium locum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 1, 15, 142</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
